description:
Make a citation handle, `emem:fact:<cell64>:<fact_cid>` (or `:<state_cid>`). Any agent or LLM resolves it to the same signed object, byte for byte. Give this one string to another agent instead of a new description of the fact. The tool checks that both parts are not empty and do not contain the `:` separator. Memory algebra: the `cite` operation (https://emem.dev/docs/model.html).

When to use: Call this when you need one string that cites a place and an attested fact across messages, agents or tools. Use `emem_echo_verify` before you publish the value. FOR MANY FACTS, USE emem_memory_bundle. This is a measured result. A token is 83 to 84 characters and 51 LLM tokens. The value it cites is 11 characters and 5.4 tokens on average. Thus N tokens use about 9.5 times the context of the N numbers. A bundle is 38 characters for any N up to 256, and it resolves in one round trip. It costs less than tokens from N=1, and less than the plain values from N=5. Use one token to cite ONE fact that you must verify later.

Example arguments: {"cell":"defi.zb493.xoso.zcb6a","fact_cid":"cxjiu7l54ujzrpnekp24n4534yojpue4mprddbvevnqtti3lh5bq"}
